-- title:
--   Lemma 4.2: one-step change of $\mathcal L_\gamma$
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $(P)$ is the problem $\min\, G(u,v) + J(u) + H(v)$ subject to $\Theta(u) + Bv = 0$, $u \in U$, $v \in \mathbb{R}^d$, with data satisfying Assumption 1, the algorithm parameters $K, \beta, L_K, \gamma, \sigma$ satisfy Assumption 2 and $0 < \sigma < 1$, and $\{w^k\} = \{(u^k, v^k, p^k)\}$ is a sequence generated by NAPP-AL with step parameters $\sigma\delta_k \le \epsilon^k \le \delta_k$, where $\delta_k$ is set as in (8).
--
--   Write $L_\Omega = \sum_j L_{\Omega_j}$ and $\lambda = \lambda_{\min}(B^\top B)$. Then:
--
--   1. for every $k \ge 1$,
--   $$\begin{aligned}\mathcal L_\gamma(u^{k+1},v^{k+1},p^k) - \mathcal L_\gamma(u^k,v^k,p^k) \le{}& -\Big(\frac{\beta}{2\epsilon^k} - \frac{L_G + \|q^k\|L_\Omega + \gamma(L^0_\Theta)^2}{2}\Big)\|u^k - u^{k+1}\|^2 - \frac{\gamma\lambda - (L_G + L_H)}{2}\|v^k - v^{k+1}\|^2 \\ &+ \frac{1}{2\gamma}\big(\|p^{k-1} - p^k\|^2 - \|p^k - p^{k+1}\|^2\big) + \frac1\gamma\|p^k - p^{k+1}\|^2 ;\end{aligned}$$
--   2. for every $k \ge 0$,
--   $$\mathcal L_\gamma(u^{k+1},v^{k+1},p^{k+1}) - \mathcal L_\gamma(u^{k+1},v^{k+1},p^k) = \frac1\gamma\|p^k - p^{k+1}\|^2 ;$$
--   3. for every $k \ge 1$,
--   $$\begin{aligned}\mathcal L_\gamma(w^{k+1}) - \mathcal L_\gamma(w^k) \le{}& -\Big(\frac{\beta}{2\epsilon^k} - \frac{L_G + \|q^k\|L_\Omega + \gamma(L^0_\Theta)^2}{2}\Big)\|u^k - u^{k+1}\|^2 - \frac{\gamma\lambda - (L_G + L_H)}{2}\|v^k - v^{k+1}\|^2 + \frac{1}{2\gamma}\big(\|p^{k-1} - p^k\|^2 - \|p^k - p^{k+1}\|^2\big) \\ &+ \frac{6\gamma\|B\|^2(L^0_\Theta)^2}{\lambda}\|u^k - u^{k+1}\|^2 + \frac{6(L_G + \gamma\|B\|L^0_\Theta)^2}{\gamma\lambda}\|u^{k-1} - u^k\|^2 + \frac{6(L_G + L_H)^2}{\gamma\lambda}\|v^{k-1} - v^k\|^2 .\end{aligned}$$
--
--   These estimates are the descent inequalities from which the potential $\Lambda^k$ of (18) is built.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: (H1), (H2): G : ℝⁿ×ℝᵈ → (−∞,+∞] and H : ℝᵈ → (−∞,+∞] with convex domains and gradients Lipschitz on their domains → G, H real-valued and differentiable on all of ℝⁿ×ℝᵈ and ℝᵈ, with globally L_G-, L_H-Lipschitz gradients; reason: §1.1 (p. 2) declares G : Rn × Rd → R and H : Rd → R; with extended values step (6), which minimizes over all of ℝᵈ, can return a point where ∇H does not exist (paper.md Reading 2)
--   - reading: §1.1 (p. 2): J : Rn → R is lower semi-continuous → J : ℝⁿ → (−∞, +∞] (never −∞), l.s.c. on dom J, dom J convex when U = ℝⁿ, locally Lipschitz on dom J ∩ U, exactly as in (H3); reason: (H3) of Assumption 1 (p. 7), under which every result is stated, gives J the codomain (−∞, ∞] and l.s.c. on dom(J) only; Lean follows (H3), which contains p. 2's real-valued l.s.c. J as a special case
--   - encoding: (H6): B is a tall matrix; the proof of Lemma 4.2 (p. 14) uses the full column rank of B in (H6) → 0 < lamMin B, i.e. λ_min(BᵀB) > 0; reason: full column rank is λ_min(BᵀB) > 0; Assumption 2(ii) divides by λ_min(BᵀB), so the condition only excludes instances where the source's statement is undefined (Reading 6)
--   - encoding: J proper (Definition 2.1 and Definition 6.1 are for proper functions; (12)–(14) subtract J-values) → ∃ u ∈ U, J u ≠ ⊤ (dom J ∩ U ≠ ∅); reason: this is properness of L_γ + I_U; without it every value of L̃_γ is +∞ and the paper's objects are undefined (Reading 7)
--   - encoding: L_G, L_H, L⁰_Θ, L_{Ω_j}, L_K are Lipschitz constants → given real numbers with 0 ≤ L and the Lipschitz inequality; reason: a Lipschitz constant is a nonnegative number; nonnegativity only matters when a space is trivial
--   - reading: statements that involve w^{k−1} (no range of k given) → stated for every k ≥ 1; reason: w^{k−1} exists only for k ≥ 1, and u⁰ ∈ ℝⁿ is arbitrary, so (12) with u = u^k needs u^k ∈ U, i.e. k ≥ 1 (Reading 8)
--   - encoding: differences of values of L_γ (or Λ^k), e.g. a − b ≤ c → additive form a ≤ b + c in EReal; reason: L_γ takes values in (−∞,+∞]; the two forms agree whenever b is finite, which holds at the iterates with k ≥ 1
-- source:
--   Zhu, Zhao, Zhang, A First-Order Primal-Dual Method for Nonconvex Constrained Optimization Based on the Augmented Lagrangian, arXiv:2007.12219v1, Lemma 4.2, pp. 11–12

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_VPEB_W
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_VPEB_Problem
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_VPEB_Assumption1
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_VPEB_Params
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_VPEB_Assumption2
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_VPEB_IsNAPPAL
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_VPEB_lamMin
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_VPEB_augLag
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_VPEB_qk

open scoped InnerProductSpace Topology

namespace NAPPAL.VPEB

/-- **Lemma 4.2, statements (i)–(iii): one-step change of `L_γ`.**
Zhu, Zhao, Zhang, *A First-Order Primal-Dual Method for Nonconvex Constrained Optimization
Based on the Augmented Lagrangian*, arXiv:2007.12219v1, Lemma 4.2, pp. 11–12: "Suppose that Assumptions 1 and 2 hold. Suppose that the sequence
{w^k} is generated by NAPP-AL. Then the following estimations hold true:
(i) Lγ(u^{k+1}, v^{k+1}, p^k) − Lγ(u^k, v^k, p^k) ≤ −(β/(2ε^k) − (LG + ‖q^k‖LΩ + γ(L0Θ)²)/2)
‖u^k − u^{k+1}‖² − ((γλmin(B⊤B) − (LG + LH))/2)‖v^k − v^{k+1}‖² + (1/(2γ))(‖p^{k−1} − p^k‖²
− ‖p^k − p^{k+1}‖²) + (1/γ)‖p^k − p^{k+1}‖².
(ii) Lγ(u^{k+1}, v^{k+1}, p^{k+1}) − Lγ(u^{k+1}, v^{k+1}, p^k) = (1/γ)‖p^k − p^{k+1}‖².
(iii) Lγ(u^{k+1}, v^{k+1}, p^{k+1}) − Lγ(u^k, v^k, p^k) ≤ −(β/(2ε^k) − (LG + ‖q^k‖LΩ +
γ(L0Θ)²)/2)‖u^k − u^{k+1}‖² − ((γλmin(B⊤B) − (LG + LH))/2)‖v^k − v^{k+1}‖² + (1/(2γ))
(‖p^{k−1} − p^k‖² − ‖p^k − p^{k+1}‖²) + (6γ‖B‖²(L0Θ)²/λmin(B⊤B))‖u^k − u^{k+1}‖² +
(6(LG + γ‖B‖L0Θ)²/(γλmin(B⊤B)))‖u^{k−1} − u^k‖² + (6(LG + LH)²/(γλmin(B⊤B)))‖v^{k−1} − v^k‖²."

(i) and (iii), which involve `p^{k−1}` and `w^{k−1}`, hold for every `k ≥ 1`; (ii) holds for
every `k`.

The standing hypotheses are those of the whole analysis: `P` satisfies Assumption 1 (with the
standing hypotheses of (P)), `A` satisfies Assumption 2 (with the parameter ranges of the
NAPP-AL box), and `w` (with step parameters `ε`) is generated by NAPP-AL with `δ_k` as in (8).

**Formalization Note.** `L_γ` takes values in `(−∞, +∞]`, so each "`a − b ≤ c`" is written in
the additive form `a ≤ b + c` (and (ii) as `a = b + c`), which is the same statement whenever
`b` is finite; for `k ≥ 1` all values involved are finite (`u^k, u^{k+1} ∈ U` minimize (5), and
`J + I_U` is proper). `L_Ω = Σ_j L_{Ω_j}`; `q^k = qk P A w k`; `ε^k = ε k`. -/
theorem lemma_4_2 {n d m : ℕ} (P : Problem n d m) (hP : Assumption1 P) (A : Params n)
    (hA : Assumption2 P A) (w : ℕ → W n d m) (ε : ℕ → ℝ) (hw : IsNAPPAL P A w ε) :
    (∀ k : ℕ, 1 ≤ k →
      augLag P A.γ (w (k + 1)).fst.fst (w (k + 1)).fst.snd (w k).snd ≤
        augLag P A.γ (w k).fst.fst (w k).fst.snd (w k).snd +
          ((-(A.β / (2 * ε k) -
                (P.LG + ‖qk P A w k‖ * (∑ j, P.LΩj j) + A.γ * P.L0Θ ^ 2) / 2) *
                ‖(w k).fst.fst - (w (k + 1)).fst.fst‖ ^ 2 -
              (A.γ * lamMin P.B - (P.LG + P.LH)) / 2 *
                ‖(w k).fst.snd - (w (k + 1)).fst.snd‖ ^ 2 +
              1 / (2 * A.γ) *
                (‖(w (k - 1)).snd - (w k).snd‖ ^ 2 - ‖(w k).snd - (w (k + 1)).snd‖ ^ 2) +
              1 / A.γ * ‖(w k).snd - (w (k + 1)).snd‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : EReal)) ∧
    (∀ k : ℕ,
      augLag P A.γ (w (k + 1)).fst.fst (w (k + 1)).fst.snd (w (k + 1)).snd =
        augLag P A.γ (w (k + 1)).fst.fst (w (k + 1)).fst.snd (w k).snd +
          ((1 / A.γ * ‖(w k).snd - (w (k + 1)).snd‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : EReal)) ∧
    (∀ k : ℕ, 1 ≤ k →
      augLag P A.γ (w (k + 1)).fst.fst (w (k + 1)).fst.snd (w (k + 1)).snd ≤
        augLag P A.γ (w k).fst.fst (w k).fst.snd (w k).snd +
          ((-(A.β / (2 * ε k) -
                (P.LG + ‖qk P A w k‖ * (∑ j, P.LΩj j) + A.γ * P.L0Θ ^ 2) / 2) *
                ‖(w k).fst.fst - (w (k + 1)).fst.fst‖ ^ 2 -
              (A.γ * lamMin P.B - (P.LG + P.LH)) / 2 *
                ‖(w k).fst.snd - (w (k + 1)).fst.snd‖ ^ 2 +
              1 / (2 * A.γ) *
                (‖(w (k - 1)).snd - (w k).snd‖ ^ 2 - ‖(w k).snd - (w (k + 1)).snd‖ ^ 2) +
              6 * A.γ * ‖P.B‖ ^ 2 * P.L0Θ ^ 2 / lamMin P.B *
                ‖(w k).fst.fst - (w (k + 1)).fst.fst‖ ^ 2 +
              6 * (P.LG + A.γ * ‖P.B‖ * P.L0Θ) ^ 2 / (A.γ * lamMin P.B) *
                ‖(w (k - 1)).fst.fst - (w k).fst.fst‖ ^ 2 +
              6 * (P.LG + P.LH) ^ 2 / (A.γ * lamMin P.B) *
                ‖(w (k - 1)).fst.snd - (w k).fst.snd‖ ^ 2 : ℝ) : EReal)) := by sorry

end NAPPAL.VPEB
